{"key":"f57736a139b636f2","source_file":"Potts Bl - Bu.json","source_id":31150,"source_url":"concordance-bridle-ppl-fraenum","term":"Bridle","headwords":["Bridle"],"latin":["Fraenum","Fraenare"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Bridle"],"latin":["Fraenum","Fraenare"]}],"header_sentences":["See Check."],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AC","AE","AR"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"6832","subsection":"10"},"text":"When the rein is given to their cupidities... AC 7375. AC 7875. AC 8295. AC 8678. AC 10814:2. HH 559. HH 562. NJHD 71. DP 231:7.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"6977","subsection":"end"},"text":"Kept in check by fear...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"10808","subsection":null},"text":"So that good... bridled evil...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AR","section":"653","subsection":null},"text":"The bridles of the horses () = the truths of the Word, by which the understanding is led. Explained, Illustrated.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"923","subsection":null},"text":"The bridles of the horses = government and dominion, for he who sits on a horse rules and masters it by the bridle.","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"bridle","url":"/meta/potts/bridle/"}